    "raw_html": "<div id=\"question-122482\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">5.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/703#5674\">Calculating the Number of Permutations of Objects Chosen From a Group of at Least Ten</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"122482\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Mary has twelve different types of fruits. If she wants to choose three fruits without repetition, one for breakfast, one for lunch, and one for dinner, how many possible permutations of fruits does she have to choose from?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Mon, Oct 5th @ 9:10 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:14</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
